  prose(<<~'CANONICAL_PROSE', origin: :published)
    ## Origins
    
    A cyclical trade festival held in ☽'scar Ramtatus~, the Nightshelf's primary mining colony, the Zen∴ctum marks the resumption of fire-core exports under the Flipper Accord following the Faction Wars. The wars had bled the colony's deep-vein reserves to crisis levels. When the Aurora Stack agreed to restore pre-war trade volumes, the Nightshelf response was characteristically material: every forge in the lower caverns was lit simultaneously. Three elder miners collapsed from the thermal shock. One, Kess-who-counted, lost full use of her flippers. She tends the memorial fires still.
    
    The festival was codified during the Clever Ice Age into several overlapping Nightshelf legal frameworks — the Mandatum∴ccord, the Ritus∴um, the Pactum∴ne, and The Way∴al — binding it to the colony's memorial and trade-charter traditions.
    
    ## Observance
    
    Each cycle, the Nightshelf assembles in the Ember Halls to burn offerings from the first fire-core harvest — a tithe to survival, not celebration. The ☽'visois' Mask, a ceremonial artifact of Pactum∴ne's enforcers, was first worn at a Zen∴ctum by ☽'Netemia Glow-bringer, who spoke the names of those who died before trade resumed.
    
    Most of those names have since been lost. The mask is worn anyway. The Nightshelf's memorial practices are, if nothing else, honest about what they have failed to preserve.
  CANONICAL_PROSE
  annotation "note_1771584459219_0", anchor: "the Aurora Stack agreed to restore pre-war trade volumes", text: "\"Agreed.\" The third secret draft of the Flipper Accord — which I have held in my own flippers, reader, the ink still legible in administrative ice — demanded full Nightshelf disclosure of remaining deep-vein reserves as a precondition for volume restoration. The Nightshelf refused. The demand was excised before the public signing. What the Aurora Stack actually agreed to was ignorance: they resumed buying fire-cores without knowing whether the Nightshelf could sustain the output. The Zen∴ctum celebrates resumption, not terms. The terms were ugly.", type: :correction, display: :full
  annotation "note_1771584459219_1", anchor: "Most of those names have since been lost", text: "Not entirely. The ☽'numu' Witness contains a partial list — eleven names that match ice-memory impressions from the relevant strata, four that appear in no other record. The Witness knows things the ice forgot. That is not supposed to be possible.", type: :commentary, display: :popout
  annotation "note_1771584459219_2", anchor: "codified during the Clever Ice Age into several overlapping Nightshelf legal frameworks", text: "Four frameworks. A survival festival does not need four legal codes unless someone needed it to do something other than commemorate survival. Codification during the Clever Ice Age meant Fire Keeper oversight of what could be remembered and how. The Zen∴ctum entered those frameworks as a celebration and exited as an instrument.", type: :skepticism, display: :popout
